@startuml t10-mcp-tool-call
title MCP Tools: Discovery, Selection, and Execution
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

participant "Model" as model #lightyellow
participant "AI Host" as host #aliceblue
participant "MCP Client" as client #lightblue
participant "MCP Server" as server #palegreen
participant "Users Management\nService" as api #mistyrose

== Discovery (after initialization) ==
host -> client : Discover available tools
client -> server : tools/list
server --> client : Tool definitions and JSON Schemas
client --> host : Available tools
host -> model : User request and tool definitions

== Selection and Policy ==
model --> host : Propose get_user_by_id(user_id: 999)
host -> host : Apply permissions and approval policy
note over host, client #lightyellow
  Invocation proceeds only if permitted.
end note
host -> client : Invoke approved tool call
client -> server : tools/call (id: 5)
server -> server : Validate request and access

== Alternative Outcomes ==
alt Tool succeeds
  server -> api : Fetch user 999
  api --> server : User record
  server --> client : result.content + isError: false
else Tool operation fails
  server -> api : Fetch user 999
  api --> server : Service unavailable
  server --> client : result.content + isError: true
else Protocol handling fails
  server --> client : error.code + error.message
end
client --> host : Correlated response (id: 5)
host -> model : Tool result, or handled failure context
model --> host : User-facing answer

note over client, server #lightcyan
  HTTP transport failures are a separate layer.
  A response has either result or error, never both.
end note
@enduml